<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<para>Complete the table using all of the exponent properties you learned in the lesson.</para>
<table>
  <tgroup cols="2"><caption>Exponent Property Review</caption>
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry>Expression</entry>
      <entry>Simplified Result</entry>
      </row>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      <row>
      <entry>
        \(j^5 \cdot j^3\)
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       \(\frac{h^7}{h^3}\)
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       \((-ab)^0\)
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \(\frac{1}{s^{-4}}\)
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \((\frac{m}{n})^{-4}\)
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       \((p^5)^2\)
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \((3s^3t^2)^3\)
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
      \((\frac{b}{d})^{-2}\)
      </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</tgroup></table>
<para class="os-raise-text-bold">Answer:</para>
<table>
  <tgroup cols="2"><caption>Exponent Property Review</caption>
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry>Expression</entry>
      <entry>Simplified Result</entry>
      </row>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>
       \(j^5 \cdot j^3\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
        \(j^8\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \(\frac{h^7}{h^3}\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
       \(h^4\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       \((-ab)^0\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
      \(1\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \(\frac{1}{s^{-4}}\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
       \(s^4\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       \((\frac{m}{n})^{-4}\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
       \(\frac{n^4}{m^4}\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
      \((p^5)^2\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
      \(p^{10}\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       \((3s^3t^2)^3\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
       \(3^3s^9t^6 = 27s^9t^6\)
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        \((\frac{b}{d})^{-2}\)
      </entry>
      <entry>
        \(\frac{d^2}{b^2}\)
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</tgroup></table>
<para>Take some time to review each of the exponential properties you learned in the lesson. Look at each property and be sure you know when to use it.</para>
<div class="os-raise-graybox os-raise-text-center">
  <para class="os-raise-text-bold"> Summary of Exponent Properties</para>
    <hr/>
  <para>If \(a\) and \(b\) are real numbers and \(m\) and \(n\) are integers, then</para>
  <table>
    <tgroup cols="2"><thead>
      <row>
        <entry>Property</entry>
        <entry>Description</entry>
      </row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>  
        <entry>
          Product Property
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(a^m \cdot a^n={a^{m+n}}\) 
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
        Power Property
        </entry>
        <entry>
        \((a^m)^n=a^{m·n}\) 
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
        Product to a Power
        </entry>
        <entry>
        \((ab)^m=a^mb^m\) 
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
        Quotient Property
        </entry>
        <entry>
        \(\frac{a^m}{a^n}=a^{m−n}\), \(a\neq0\) 
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
        Zero Exponent Property
        </entry>
        <entry>
        \(a^0=1\), \(a\neq0\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          Quotient to a Power Property
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \((\frac{a}{b})^m=\frac{a^m}{b^m}\), \(b\neq0\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
         Properties of Negative Exponents
        </entry>
        <entry>
         \(a^{−n}=\frac{1}{a^n}\) and \(\frac{1}{a^{−n}}=a^n\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          Quotient to a Negative Exponent
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \((\frac{a}{b})^{−n}=(\frac{b}{a})^n\)
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </tgroup></table>
</div></section>
</content>
